From: Shane de Deuge <shane@scielex.com.au>
Subject: [PATCH] iio: light: opt3001: add the OPT3002, from mainline

The mangOH Yellow's light sensor is an OPT3002: the OPT3001's registers, without the device ID,
reading optical power at 1.2 nW/cm^2 a count. This is mainline's driver (linux-6.18.y), which reports
it as in_intensity_raw, changed only for kernel 4.14's I2C probe, remove and event signatures.

Upstream-Status: Backport [mainline drivers/iio/light/opt3001.c, adapted to kernel 4.14]
